{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -A 38 -B 3 'D494|D495' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"5638-  `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/record/RECORD-TEST-DESIGN.md`: the kept figures assembled by code into a company record, read for\n5639-  fidelity and for whether a reader can answer six fixed questions from it. Any change to what the product shows or sends stays Alex's.\n5640-\n5641:## D494 · 2026-11-14 · The kept figures as a company record: close, not ready; who a figure is from is stored per statement; three choices to Alex (council consensus)\n5642-\n5643-- **Test** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/record/RECORD-TEST-DESIGN.md`, `RECORD-TEST-RESULT.md`; $0; design changed twice by the council\n5644-  before any row was read): the clean week draw's 341 kept figure rows assembled by code; fidelity read by two blind reader families on 20\n5645-  rows of each stratum; six fixed questions answered by a blind reader from the record of 40 articles alone, against a reference written\n5646-  from the same articles, compared blind.\n5647-- **Result:** measure and value right in all 40 rows read; no period wrong; revenue and margin rows 0 wrong of 20. From the record alone the\n5648-  reader gave the same answers as the reference on five of six questions. **The usability line is missed** on one wrong statement: the\n5649-  record gives the reported 75% gross margin as the CFO's, because who and when are stored once per statement and that statement also held\n5650-  her two outlook figures. Unsettled: the other rows' fidelity (1 wrong by both families; 2 on which the families differ over \"Consensus\n5651-  analysts\"; 1 mark traced to the readers' packet lacking the publisher), and the completeness of two questions' comparison.\n5652-- **Counted** (Claude's reading, a floor): 15 of 179 statements hold figures of more than one kind (50 rows); in 5 of them a figure is not\n5653-  the statement's party's (at least 6 rows: the market's estimate under the company's or the CFO's name is the commonest). Periods of the\n5654-  186 revenue and margin rows: mostly written fiscal forms a parser could unite; about 42 relative or missing. 44 rows of the view fell\n5655-  under 42 headings.\n5656-- **Council** (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mx-codex-4.md`, `mx-codex-5.md`): \"Take the three choices to Alex, leaning toward\n5657-  testing per-figure source and period fields because the stored attribution itself can combine different speakers. Present that as an\n5658-  unproven new version with safeguards, and correct or qualify the attribution census before quoting its total.\"\n5659-- **To Alex** (it changes what the system stores or shows): (1) a new version of the clean Step 1 request in which each kept figure carries\n5660-  its own source and a period in a fixed form, tested on stored states with guards and then by this record test on unread articles (the\n5661-  council's and Claude's lean, unproven); (2) the request unchanged, a neutral display tested on unread articles at no cost; (3) leave the\n5662-  record, and take him the standing-question comparison (presets, D370) or turn back to the current system. Nothing is sent before he\n5663-  answers.\n5664-\n5665:## D495 · 2026-11-14 · Alex opens a new version of the clean Step 1 record: each kept figure carries its own source and a fixed-form period\n5666-\n5667:- **Asked** (after D494, his reply to this exact question): \"复盘后我用新系统已经留下的财务数字拼了一份公司财务记录并做了盲评：数字本身都准（40 条抽查全对），读者只看记录能答对六个问题里的五个，\n5668-  但有一处把数字安错了人（75% 毛利率被记成 CFO 说的）。原因是新系统按“一条事实”记一次说话人，而一条事实里常有好几个数字。下一步走哪条？\" Options: a new version in which each figure\n5669-  carries its source (recommended); the request unchanged, display only; leave the line.\n5670-- **Alex:** \"开新版：每个数字自带来源 (Recommended)\". The option as shown to him: \"开一个新版本的第一步，让每个数字自己带上来源和固定格式的期间（只加字段，不改开题和挂靠规则）。先在已存文章\n5671-  上测并守住现有行为，再用没看过的文章重做记录测试，约 1 美元。没有证明一定有效。\"\n5672-- **Decided:** a test arm of the clean Step 1 request (c21) whose only difference from the adopted c8 is two fields on each figure of a kept\n5673-  statement: whose figure it is, and its period in a fixed form. No opening, linking or keeping rule changes; c8 stays the adopted request\n5674-  until a result is adopted. First a probe on stored states with guards on what the request decides today, its lines and stop written\n5675-  before any send and a council round before the send; then the record test on unread articles, only if the probe passes.\n5676-\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -A 85 '\"'^## 17[. :]|''^### 17[. :]'\"' clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md\"","aggregated_output":"472:## 17. Alex decides the shape (2026-11-08)\n473-\n474-On the recommendation \"keep a useful financial figure that no view takes in the company's conditions record, labelled actual,\n475-guidance or expectation, with who said it and the period; it becomes evidence when a related view opens and the reference when views\n476-are judged\", against the alternative \"drop it as D209 does now\", **Alex replied: \"好\".**\n477-\n478-**Decided:**\n479-1. Financial figures are not theses on their own; a thesis is a view with a reason.\n480-2. A useful company financial figure that no view takes is kept as a condition, not dropped. This amends D209 for such figures only;\n481-   other no-home statements are still dropped.\n482-\n483-**Next:** the conditions design (`clean-arch/STEP1-CONDITIONS-DESIGN.md`), council review until a round finds nothing serious, then a\n484-small probe.\n485-\n486-## 18. Conditions design: passed the design gate (2026-11-08)\n487-\n488-`clean-arch/STEP1-CONDITIONS-DESIGN.md` went through eight review rounds, each by a fresh, independent Codex session: v1 `m-codex.md`,\n489-v2 to v8 `n-` to `t-codex.md`.\n490-\n491-**What the rounds changed:**\n492-- **v2:** a condition became an optional `condition` object on an evidence item, not a separate record, so every existing check and the\n493-  Step 2 and Step 3 paths are reused. Only a condition with no links is kept instead of dropped.\n494-- **v3:**\n495-  - an entity-wide, evidence-only search for items with no thesis (otherwise a repeat would be saved as new);\n496-  - the field hand-off fixed (separate date fields);\n497-  - `balance` folded into actual.\n498-- **v4:**\n499-  - complete backfill with a judged-pair ledger and recovery;\n500-  - one view definition, which includes competitive position;\n501-  - draw rules fixed.\n502-- **v5:**\n503-  - numeric boundaries on the value check;\n504-  - anchors that test Alex's margin, supplier and cash rulings as decided.\n505-- **v6:** identity split from meaning. Code checks that a figure is quoted; readers check that it is paired with the right measure,\n506-  with a 2% bar.\n507-- **v7:** condition fields kept out of Step 2 by construction, with an isolation test.\n508-- **v8:** Step 2's 600-character passage cut removed. It cut 44 of 282 stored items (16%), a latent defect of the existing Step 2 for\n509-  evidence too, so Step 2's lines will be re-measured.\n510-\n511-**Round 8:** \"没有发现其他会使这次探针结果无法解释或导致构建错误的严重设计问题\". The only remaining blockers are the prerequisites,\n512-which are build work:\n513-1. the scorer test;\n514-2. the value-check real-data report;\n515-3. the backfill tests;\n516-4. the isolation and full-passage test;\n517-5. the independent review of `anchors.json` and the rubric.\n518-\n519-**Next:** build them and the c1 arm, then probe 3c, about $1.25.\n520-\n521-## 19. Build for probe 4 (conditions, c1); Alex: no scorer (2026-11-08)\n522-\n523-**Alex:** \"不要写评分器这个之前就出问题过，你自己读trace 来分析\". Written into AGENTS §7.2. The probe is judged by Claude reading every\n524-answer against `anchors.json` (fixed before the send). The design's scorer prerequisite and its reader-family scoring are dropped.\n525-\n526-**Sequencing.** Probe 4 is Step 1 only (fixed states). The Step 2 and 3 changes (no-thesis search, full passages, backfill) and their\n527-tests are built before the forward run, not before this probe, because this probe does not exercise them.\n528-\n529-**Built:**\n530-- `clean-arch/step1/runner.py`: optional `condition` on evidence items.\n531-  - `figure_in_passages`: the value is quoted in one verified passage, with numeric boundaries.\n532-  - An invalid condition is removed, with the reason in `condition_issues`.\n533-  - **A valid condition with empty links is kept**, not unfiled.\n534-  - 3 tests; all 4 mutants caught (condition does not keep; no left boundary; no right boundary; invalid condition kept).\n535-- **Arm c1** (`arms/c1-*`, against k6b):\n536-  - the role paragraph and a new §2 CONDITION bullet (the company's own figures carry a condition and are kept with empty links when\n537-    no thesis takes them; target prices, the share price and other companies' figures are not conditions);\n538-  - §3 now reads \"a thesis is a view: a question whose answer turns on a reason …; a financial figure on its own is not a view\";\n539-  - big matters read \"a reason that can move the quantities that carry the company's value\";\n540-  - the do-not-open list reads \"a financial measure's level, growth or guidance with no reason (it is a condition)\", plus \"a measure\n541-    with a reason the item supports is a view (margins fall because input costs cannot be passed on)\";\n542-  - one closing-check sentence;\n543-  - the schema gains `condition`.\n544-  - System prompt +905 characters (+6.7%). **Growth reason:** the new conditions contract Alex decided needs its definition; it is not\n545-    a patch.\n546-- A synthetic c1 answer passes every check: 1 condition kept with empty links, 0 issues.\n547-\n548-**Probe 4:** c1 on the 16 cases, 3 draws, 48 sends, about $0.50. **The control is probe 3's same-day k6b draws.**\n549-\n550-## 20. Probe 4 read (c1 against the same-day k6b control): mixed; three mechanisms traced to c1's own sentences (2026-11-08)\n551-\n552-**What was run.** 16 cases × 3 draws, 48 sends, $0.67. One c1 answer failed the format check (`condition` missing on one item); the\n553-control had 0 of 48. **The control** is probe 3's same-day k6b draws. Every answer was read against `anchors.json`, which was fixed\n554-before the send. The frozen-gold table from the existing scorer (`score_probe.py`) was used as a lead only; no scorer was written.\n555-\n556-**What c1 fixed (read per answer):**\n557-\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; from pathlib import Path; p=Path(\\\"clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms\\\"); a=json.loads((p/\\\"c8-schema.json\\\").read_text()); b=json.loads((p/\\\"c21-schema.json\\\").read_text()); x=b[\\\"properties\\\"][\\\"evidence\\\"][\\\"items\\\"][\\\"properties\\\"][\\\"figures\\\"][\\\"items\\\"]; x[\\\"required\\\"]=[k for k in x[\\\"required\\\"] if k not in (\\\"party\\\",\\\"fiscal_period\\\")]; [x[\\\"properties\\\"].pop(k) for k in (\\\"party\\\",\\\"fiscal_period\\\")]; print(\\\"Only two additions:\\\",a==b);'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
